{
  "dom_id": "step-q127464",
  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(7,-1,0)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,1,-4⟩.$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{1}=\\frac{z-0}{-4}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z}{-4}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
